<section class="section" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <p class="section__eyebrow reveal">About</p>
  <h2 class="section__title reveal" id="about-title">Hi, I’m Ben.</h2>

  <div class="about-layout">
    <div class="about-body reveal">
      <p>
        I began my clinical practice as a Music Therapist before training further
        in Integrative Psychotherapy. I am based in Walthamstow, Waltham Forest
        (E17), working with individuals who are carrying deep-rooted trauma or
        navigating complex emotional and mental health difficulties—with a strong
        focus on adolescents and young adults.
      </p>
      <p>
        Core to my practice is the belief that “therapy resistance” is a myth;
        usually, it just means the right framework hasn’t been offered yet. I
        integrate Acceptance and Commitment Therapy (ACT) to help clients find
        flexible, realistic keys to engagement and meaningful change.
      </p>
      <p>
        When we work together, you can expect candour, collaboration, and a space
        where your lived experience is held in higher regard than textbook models.
        I’m interested in functional truth: the underlying beliefs we treat as true
        and act upon—even when they cause us pain—and how those beliefs drive our
        behaviour day-to-day. I may invite you to try new ways of exploring these
        patterns in sessions, but always in your own time, at your own pace, and
        with clear consent.
      </p>
      <p>
        (And if you’d like, my rescue dog Pru can also make an appearance in our sessions.)
      </p>
    </div>

